{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves-onroad",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.40: the onroad CATALOGUE of a DEFAULT-domain run -- every RunSpec in `runspecs/` but `scale-project` mounts this. It declares the run's DOMAIN and the tables whose merged content depends on it, and mounts `onroad/default-database.esm` for the default database's other 82 tables and the model. A per-fixture document mounts THIS and supplies its RunSpec's selections and its oracle.\n\nWHY THE CATALOGUE IS TWO LAYERS. Until step 7f this file was the whole catalogue, and it could stay one layer only while every run read the default database alone. MOVES merges a SINGLE-county or PROJECT run's scale-input database first and the default database after it, and skips the default's copy of some tables altogether in some domains -- `Link` in PROJECT domain, `FuelSupply` and `IMCoverage` in SINGLE and PROJECT (InputDataManager.java:1432-1435, :2799-2846). A mounting document cannot override a mounted one's `data_sources` (docs/esm-conventions.md §59.4), so those tables are declared one level ABOVE the default database, by a document per domain: this one for DEFAULT, one per scale-input database in `inputs/` for the others (§92). Two are here today, because two are all `scale-project` needed: `link` and `linkSourceTypeHour`.\n\nWHAT A DEFAULT-DOMAIN RUN READS FOR THEM is the default database's own: the national `Link`, one synthetic link per county and road type, and the empty `linkSourceTypeHour`. And `runspecdomain`, one row, DEFAULT, which `onroad/model.esm` reads as `run_isProjectDomain` = 0 -- so ProjectTAG's SHO, the link's own operating-mode distribution and link-level output geography are all switched off, and every RunSpec that mounts this computes exactly what it did before the split, measured byte for byte on all twenty.\n\nIT ALSO RELAYS THREE METAPARAMETERS, as onroad/default-database.esm does one level down: `bindings` closes only a name the referenced document declares (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1), so `n_outputRate`, `n_sourceBin` and `n_physicsRow` are declared at every mount edge between a RunSpec and the model.\n\nIT DOES NOT LOAD ALONE, by design: it names no runspec, and run-tests.sh asserts the refusal. `./movesdb/` is an untracked symlink to the monolithic default database (§7.3.1).",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "onroad",
      "domain",
      "default-database",
      "default-domain"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_link": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/Link.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_link"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "output"
        ],
        "note": "Link, the default database's national table: 22,610 rows, one synthetic link per county and road type, with linkLength, linkVolume, linkAvgSpeed and linkAvgGrade all NULL. Declared HERE and not in onroad/default-database.esm because it is the first DOMAIN-owned table: MOVES copies it into a DEFAULT-domain run and does not copy it at all into a PROJECT one (InputDataManager.java:1432), so a project database's document declares its own instead. What the run selects from it is in the joins.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_linksourcetypehour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/linkSourceTypeHour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_linksourcetypehour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "activity"
        ],
        "note": "linkSourceTypeHour, the default database's: 0 rows. Only ProjectTAG reads it, so a DEFAULT-domain run carries it empty, and `run_domainUnported` would count a row if it ever had one. A project database's document declares its own; the default's being empty is what makes MOVES's row merge of the two the project's table alone.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecdomain": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./inputs/default-domain/runspecdomain.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecdomain"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "domain"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, modelDomain DEFAULT -- ModelDomain.java's NATIONAL_ALLOCATION, the domain every RunSpec in runspecs/ but scale-project runs. The RunSpec's `<modeldomain>` is declared by the domain document rather than the per-run one because MOVES pairs the two: a SINGLE-county or PROJECT run is the one that reads a scale-input database, and a DEFAULT one reads none. Written by tools/build-scale-input-db.py --default-domain.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_input_zoneroadtype": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./inputs/default-domain/ZoneRoadType.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_inputzoneroadtype"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "activity"
        ],
        "note": "The INPUT side of ZoneRoadType's row merge: zero rows, because a DEFAULT-domain run has no input database. Mounted empty (docs/esm-conventions.md 80) so that the merge `zrt_mergedSHOAllocFactor` writes reads the default's every value. Written by tools/build-scale-input-db.py --default-domain.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_input_hotellingactivitydistribution": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./inputs/default-domain/hotellingActivityDistribution.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_inputhotellingactivitydistribution"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "hotelling"
        ],
        "note": "The INPUT side of hotellingActivityDistribution's row merge: zero rows, for the same reason. A DEFAULT-domain hotelling run reads the default side's zone 990000.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_hotellinghoursperday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/hotellingHoursPerDay.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_hotellinghoursperday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "hotelling"
        ],
        "note": "hotellingHoursPerDay, the default database's: 0 rows. A row merge whose default side is empty is the input database's table, so the domain declares it whole; a DEFAULT-domain run has none, and AdjustHotelling leaves the default hotelling hours as they are.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_hotellinghourfraction": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/hotellingHourFraction.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_hotellinghourfraction"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "hotelling"
        ],
        "note": "hotellingHourFraction, the default database's: 0 rows. AdjustHotelling's hour-fraction block, not ported; `run_domainUnported` counts a row at a run's zone.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_hotellingagefraction": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/hotellingAgeFraction.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_hotellingagefraction"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "hotelling"
        ],
        "note": "hotellingAgeFraction, the default database's: 0 rows. Not ported; counted like hotellingHourFraction.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_hotellingmonthadjust": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/hotellingMonthAdjust.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_hotellingmonthadjust"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "hotelling"
        ],
        "note": "hotellingMonthAdjust, the default database's: 0 rows. Not ported; counted like hotellingHourFraction.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_startsperday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/startsPerDay.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_startsperday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "starts"
        ],
        "note": "startsPerDay, the default database's: 0 rows. A row merge over an empty default side is the input database's table, declared whole; a DEFAULT-domain run has none and AdjustStarts computes its daily starts from startsPerDayPerVehicle.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_input_zone": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./inputs/default-domain/Zone.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_inputzone"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "starts"
        ],
        "note": "The INPUT side of Zone's row merge: zero rows, because a DEFAULT-domain run has no input database. Written by tools/build-scale-input-db.py --default-domain.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    }
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "n_outputRate": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 375,
      "description": "How many (pollutant-process, cohort) PAIRS reach MOVESOutput, summed over the run's emitted blocks. Declared here as well as in the model it mounts for the reason the numbers around it are (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1): this is the relay that lets a per-fixture document set it. It replaces `n_outputCohort` and `n_outputPolProcess`, which between them could describe only a rectangle. 375 is `process-tirewear`'s, three blocks of 125; a run with one emitted block of 125 needs 125, `expand-fueltype-diesel` 248, `expand-sourcetype` 430 and `expand-criteria` 372. `rateSurvivorCount` recomputes it, so it is a CHECKED declaration."
    },
    "n_sourceBin": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "How many source bins the widest cohort of the run holds. Declared here as well as in the model it mounts for the reason the two numbers above it are (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1): this is the relay that lets a per-fixture document set it. 1 is right for a run whose cohorts are single-binned -- a passenger car's are, and so the bin relation is that run's cohort relation row for row -- and a run that selects a light commercial truck needs 2, a refuse truck 8. `run_sourceBinsDropped` recomputes whether the value is enough, so it is a CHECKED declaration."
    },
    "n_physicsRow": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 1,
      "description": "How many rows of `sourceusetypephysics` the run's source types select between them -- the width of the drive-cycle axis. Declared here as well as in the model it mounts for the reason the three numbers above it are (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1): this is the relay that lets a per-fixture document set it. The vehicle a drive cycle is computed for is keyed by (sourceTypeID, regClassID, model-year range), so 1 is right for a motorcycle or a passenger car, a light commercial truck alone needs 3, source types 21 and 32 together 4, and the five of `expand-sourcetype` 40. `run_physicsRowsSelected` recomputes it and `run_physicsRowsDropped` says whether it is enough, so it is a CHECKED declaration."
    },
    "n_ratesScale": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 0,
      "description": "The RunSpec's `<modelscale>`: 1 at Rates scale, 0 (the default) at inventory scale. Relayed here as `n_outputRate` is (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1), so a per-fixture document can bind it (PLAN.md §7.3.47)."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "Onroad": {
      "ref": "./onroad/default-database.esm",
      "bindings": {
        "n_outputRate": "n_outputRate",
        "n_sourceBin": "n_sourceBin",
        "n_physicsRow": "n_physicsRow",
        "n_ratesScale": "n_ratesScale"
      }
    }
  }
}
